From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:47:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 068/162] hjviewer: fields, keys and names in dialogs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U07: the access password's dialogs (A1 and P2) no longer freeze while
the password is checked. [Cancel] and Esc work all along; A1 drops a
late answer, P2 ends a ticket that comes after [Cancel]. The bar says
"확인하는 중…" beside it and has a screen reader name. [Connect]/[OK]
stay off until something is typed, and during E2's wait, whose text
counts the time left down every 30 seconds (hjvRetryAt,
hjvAccessCanSend, hjvAccessErrorNow, with tests).

U53: DialogTextField gives the field its visible name for screen
readers (the label above it is excluded, so it is read once). An error
goes right under the field through InputDecoration.error, with an
icon, the red border and a live region of its own; the help text
follows it in textSecondary at 13 px. The desktop remote ID field
keeps its name while the focus hides its hint.

U54: DialogTextField and PasswordWidget take textInputAction,
onSubmitted, autofillHints, autocorrect and enableSuggestions. The
login's ID goes on to the password, whose return logs in; both sit in
an AutofillGroup that saves only after a password login
(finishAutofillContext). The A1/P2 field submits on done, as a
visible-password keyboard without autocorrect or suggestions; a shown
password is not corrected anywhere. CustomAlertDialog keeps one focus
scope for its life, Shift+Tab goes back, and Enter submits unless a
button (or another control) has the focus, in place of the flag that
stopped Enter after any Tab.

U55: the icon-only buttons named in the review get names, from a new
HJViewer text file (hjviewer_labels.dart): the phone's session bar,
the ID's clear button, a card's menu, the login's close, the password
eye (with its state), the settings' QR and the display page's back,
the desktop's other ways to connect and a tab's close. The keyboard
button and a phone card's menu get a semantics label, not a tooltip
that would take their long press. The phone's connect arrow is left
to the home lane, which already names it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
